Course.start({"num":17,"unit":4,"slug":"m17-ir","minutes":45,"title":"El verbo ir","subtitle":"Going places, a + el = al, and ir a + infinitive","lede":"*Ir* (to go) is short and very irregular. With it you can say where you're going today and what you're going to do tomorrow.","recap":"In Unit 3 you learned regular -ar, -er and -ir verbs, questions, **tener**, **estar**, and when to use **ser** or **estar**.","context":{"title":"Más lejos","place":"Javier, Navarra · Lisboa · Goa · Japón","text":"**Francisco de Javier** was born in 1506 in the castle of Javier, in northern Spain. At the University of Paris he shared a room with a student from the Basque Country, **Ignacio de Loyola**, and became one of the first Jesuits.\n\nOn **April 7, 1541**, his 35th birthday, Francisco sailed from Lisbon for India. The trip took more than a year. Over the next ten years he traveled to India, Sri Lanka, Malaysia, Indonesia and **Japan**, learning bits of new languages, teaching and caring for the sick. He died in 1552 on a small island off the coast of China, still hoping to go further.\n\nFrancisco never stopped asking: *¿Adónde voy ahora?* (*Where am I going now?*) Today he is the patron saint of missionaries. {{Francisco va a la India. Va a Japón. Va a ir a China.}}"},"learn":[{"title":"The forms of ir","text":"**Ir** looks nothing like its infinitive, but its endings look like *-ar* endings.","conj":[{"inf":"ir","en":"to go","forms":["voy","vas","va","vamos","vais","van"]}],"examples":[["¿Adónde vas? Voy a la biblioteca.","Where are you going? I'm going to the library."],["Mis padres van al trabajo.","My parents go to work."],["Vamos a casa.","We're going home."]],"tip":"*Vais* (vosotros) has no accent mark, because it's only one syllable."},{"title":"Places, and a + el = al","text":"To say *to* a place, use **a**. When **a** comes before **el**, the two words combine into **al**: {{Voy al parque.}} (never *a el*). *A la, a los, a las* don't change. And *home* is just {{a casa}}.","flash":[["la biblioteca","library"],["el parque","park"],["el cine","movie theater"],["el centro comercial","mall"],["la iglesia","church"],["el supermercado","supermarket"],["la playa","beach"],["el restaurante","restaurant"],["el gimnasio","gym"],["el museo","museum"],["el estadio","stadium"],["la piscina","swimming pool"],["el centro","downtown"],["la tienda","store"]],"tip":"The same thing happens with **de**: *de + el = **del***. {{Vengo del parque.}}"},{"title":"Ir a + infinitive: the near future","text":"**Ir a** + infinitive means *going to* do something: {{Voy a estudiar.}} (*I'm going to study.*) Only *ir* changes; the second verb stays an infinitive.\n\n**Vamos a** + infinitive can also mean *let's*: {{¡Vamos a comer!}} (*Let's eat!*) And {{¡Vamos!}} alone means *Let's go!*","examples":[["Esta noche voy a ver una película.","Tonight I'm going to watch a movie."],["Mañana vamos a jugar al fútbol.","Tomorrow we're going to play soccer."],["¿Qué vas a hacer este fin de semana?","What are you going to do this weekend?"],["La próxima semana mis primos van a venir.","Next week my cousins are going to come."]]}],"tasks":[{"id":"t1","type":"conj","title":"Conjugate ir","intro":"Write every form of *ir*.","verbs":[{"inf":"ir","en":"to go","forms":["voy","vas","va","vamos","vais","van"]}],"hints":["They all start with **v**: *voy, vas, va…*"]},{"id":"t2","type":"select","title":"Al, a la, a los or a las?","intro":"Choose the right way to say *to the*.","items":[{"s":"Voy {al|a el|a la} parque."},{"s":"Mis amigas van {a la|al|a las} playa."},{"s":"¿Vas {al|a la|a los} cine esta noche?"},{"s":"Vamos {a la|al|a las} biblioteca después de clase."},{"s":"Mi papá va {al|a la|a el} supermercado."},{"s":"Los turistas van {a los|al|a las} museos."},{"s":"Después de la escuela, voy {a casa|a la casa|al casa}.","why":"*Going home* is just **a casa**."},{"s":"Ella va {a las|a los|al} tiendas del centro."}],"hints":["**a + el = al**. Never write *a el*.","Check the noun's gender and number: *el parque → al parque*, *la playa → a la playa*."]},{"id":"t3","type":"match","title":"En la ciudad","intro":"Tap a Spanish place (you'll hear it), then its meaning.","pairs":[["el cine","movie theater"],["la biblioteca","library"],["el centro comercial","mall"],["la iglesia","church"],["la piscina","swimming pool"],["el estadio","stadium"],["la tienda","store"],["el centro","downtown"],["el museo","museum"]],"hints":["*Librería* is a bookstore; *biblioteca* is a library."]},{"id":"t4","type":"cloze","title":"What are they going to do?","intro":"Write the form of *ir* in the first blank and the infinitive in the second.","items":["Mañana yo [voy] a [estudiar] ((study)) para el examen.","Esta noche tú [vas] a [ver] ((see, watch)) una película.","El sábado mi hermana [va] a [correr] ((run)) en el parque.","Nosotros [vamos] a [comer] ((eat)) en un restaurante.","Mis abuelos [van] a [viajar] ((travel)) a México.","¿Vosotros [vais] a [escribir] ((write)) la carta?"],"hints":["The pattern is **ir** + **a** + infinitive.","The second verb is not conjugated: *voy a **estudiar***."]},{"id":"t5","type":"order","title":"Build the plans","intro":"Tap the words in order.","items":[{"en":"I'm going to the movie theater tonight.","es":"Voy al cine esta noche.","alt":["Esta noche voy al cine.","Yo voy al cine esta noche."]},{"en":"We're going to play soccer tomorrow.","es":"Vamos a jugar al fútbol mañana.","alt":["Mañana vamos a jugar al fútbol."]},{"en":"Are you going to the party?","es":"¿Vas a la fiesta?","alt":["¿Tú vas a la fiesta?"]},{"en":"Let's eat!","es":"¡Vamos a comer!","extra":["comemos"]}],"hints":["*Al* = *a* + *el*.","*Let's eat* = **vamos a** + infinitive."]},{"id":"t6","type":"listen","title":"¿Adónde van?","intro":"Listen to each person's plans. Choose the right answer.","questions":[{"say":"Esta noche voy al cine con mis amigos.","q":"Where is the speaker going tonight?","choices":[["to the movies",true],["to the mall",false],["to the gym",false],["to a friend's house",false]]},{"say":"Mañana mi familia y yo vamos a la playa.","q":"Who is going to the beach?","choices":[["the speaker and their family",true],["only the speaker",false],["only the family",false],["the speaker's friends",false]]},{"say":"El domingo mis padres van a la iglesia y después van a comer en un restaurante.","q":"What will the parents do after church?","choices":[["eat at a restaurant",true],["go shopping",false],["go to the park",false],["go home",false]]},{"say":"No voy a ir al partido porque tengo que estudiar.","q":"Why isn't the speaker going to the game?","choices":[["They have to study.",true],["They're sick.",false],["They don't like soccer.",false],["They're going to work.",false]]}],"hints":["Tap 🐢 to hear it slowly. Listen for **al** or **a la** + a place."]},{"id":"s1","type":"speak","title":"Say it out loud","intro":"Listen, record, compare.","items":[{"s":"¿Adónde vas? Voy al centro."},{"s":"Este fin de semana voy a visitar a mis abuelos."},{"s":"¡Vamos!"}]}],"build":{"heading":"Mis planes para el fin de semana","prompt":"Write **at least 5 sentences** about your plans for this weekend. Say where you're going and what you're going to do. Use **ir a** + infinitive at least **three times**, **al** or **a la** at least twice, and at least two time words (*esta noche, mañana, el sábado…*).","model":"{{Este fin de semana voy a estar muy ocupado.}} {{El sábado por la mañana voy al gimnasio.}} {{Después, mis amigos y yo vamos a comer pizza en el centro.}} {{Por la noche mi familia va a ver una película.}} {{El domingo voy a la iglesia con mis abuelos.}} {{¡No voy a estudiar!}}","placeholder":"Este fin de semana voy a…","reqs":[{"t":"At least 5 sentences","sentences":5},{"t":"**ir a** + infinitive, three times","re":"\\b(voy|vas|va|vamos|vais|van)\\s+a\\s+\\p{L}+(ar|er|ir)\\b","min":3},{"t":"**al** or **a la / a las / a los** + a place, twice","re":"\\b(al|a\\s+la|a\\s+las|a\\s+los)\\s+\\p{L}+","min":2},{"t":"Two time words","any":["hoy","mañana","esta noche","esta tarde","este fin de semana","el sábado","el domingo","el viernes","la próxima semana","por la mañana","por la tarde","por la noche","después","luego"],"min":2}]},"reflect":{"q":"Francisco Javier kept going further to meet people who needed help. Where do you hope to go in your life: a place, a job, a goal? Who might you be able to help when you get there?","placeholder":"Someday I want to go…"},"further":{"id":"x1","type":"translate","title":"Challenge: translate","items":[{"en":"Where are you (tú) going?","es":["¿adónde vas [tú]?","¿a dónde vas [tú]?"]},{"en":"She's going to the stadium.","es":["[ella] va al estadio"]},{"en":"We're going to travel to Spain.","es":["[nosotros] vamos a viajar a españa","[nosotras] vamos a viajar a españa"]},{"en":"They aren't going to go to school.","es":["[ellos] no van a ir a la escuela","[ellas] no van a ir a la escuela","[ellos] no van a ir al colegio","[ellas] no van a ir al colegio"]}]},"culture":"**¿Sabías?** Every March, thousands of people walk to the castle of Javier in Navarra for a pilgrimage called **la Javierada**, in honor of San Francisco Javier.","unitTitle":"En la ciudad: verbos irregulares","code":"MTQ1MS1SRUlWQUo=","prev":"m16-ser-estar.html","next":"m18-e-ie.html"});
